Thanks Liviu,

  I noticed (and mentioned) the user break problem (cancel button) a couple
months ago, but I figured it was just me. The rniStop function in JRI's
Rengine.c file has the following comment related to non-win32 systems:

#ifdef Win32
    UserBreak=1;
#else
 /* not really a perfect solution ... need to clarify what's the best ...*/
    kill(getpid(), SIGINT);
#endif

I was hoping that the switch over to REngine would solve this.


I agree with many of your other suggestions. Some of them shouldn't be too
hard to fix. On the plus side, the comment/uncomment problem is fixed in the
latest dev version.


Ian

