From simon.urbanek at r-project.org  Fri Jun 26 17:23:38 2009
From: simon.urbanek at r-project.org (Simon Urbanek)
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2009 13:23:38 -0400
Subject: Fwd: Hadoop rJava issue
References: <20090625183651.GA26290@gamma.logic.tuwien.ac.at>
Message-ID: <C009FADD-964C-477B-8104-3771756A282E@r-project.org>

The solution to the class-loader issues with Hadoop, courtesy of Ingo  
Feinerer:

Begin forwarded message:

> From: Ingo Feinerer
> Date: June 25, 2009 14:36:51  EDT
> Subject: Re: Hadoop rJava issue
>
> On Fri, Jun 19, 2009 at 09:54:56AM -0400, Saptarshi Guha wrote:
>> Hello,
>> Below is my conversation with Simon Urbanek. The net result is that
>> there wasn't a clean solution. As such my package does not work with
>> rJava.
>
> Thank you very much for the copy of your conversation with Simon  
> Urbanek!
>
> You might be interested that I managed to get Hadoop running with
> RJava without modifying the Hadoop Java sources. As already suspected
> by Simon Urbanek there was a class loader issue. Fortunately, I found
> a way to let Hadoop call and use the RJava class loader. Basically:
>
> configuration <- .jnew("org/apache/hadoop/conf/Configuration")
> cl <- .jclassLoader()
> configuration$setClassLoader(cl)
>
> See http://hadoop.apache.org/core/docs/current/api/org/apache/hadoop/conf/Configuration.html#setClassLoader(java.lang.ClassLoader) 
>  if you are interested in the details.
>
> Now I can access the Hadoop file system, and use the Hadoop Java API
> :-)
>
> Best regards, Ingo
>
>
> -- 
> Ingo Feinerer
> Vienna University of Technology
> http://www.dbai.tuwien.ac.at/staff/feinerer
